{"duration_api_ms":7550,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"26fbfa39-b2f2-49b4-baa6-7ef1e72e1d2b","total_cost_usd":0.0009142999999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":687,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1285,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":895},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":687,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1285,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":687,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":687},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1229,"outputTokens":1308,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":687,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0009142999999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":895,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":687,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Thresholds:** The $0.01-per-share and 0.5%-of-NAV figures are materiality triggers set by fund boards, not statutory limits. Many funds apply them as \"whichever is greater,\" though the exact wording varies by fund. An error that breaches the threshold generally requires correction and may require shareholder compensation. Errors below it are typically logged and monitored but not remediated.\n\n**Governance:** Correction is governed by the fund's board-approved valuation and pricing-error policies. These operate under Rule 38a-1 (compliance programs) and Rule 2a-5 (fair value determinations and board oversight). The administrator executes the correction and reports to the board, usually through the valuation or pricing committee. Compensation methodology and the handling of affected creations and redemptions are set in those policies. Rule 22c-1 governs the pricing of redemptions and purchases.\n\n**Practical notes for ETFs:** Errors in the NAV used for creations and redemptions affect authorized participants as well as shareholders, so the administrator should also confirm the treatment of affected transactions. Verify the exact thresholds and procedures against the specific fund's policy documents and counsel's guidance.","ttft_ms":5172,"type":"result","duration_ms":7031,"uuid":"db9338c1-c684-4aed-a157-758503e10a5b","ttft_stream_ms":816,"time_to_request_ms":53,"first_content_frame_ms":816,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
